"A clothes shop's got 40 white shirts and 50 floral ones. Half the white ones got collars, and 20 floral ones got buttons. How many more floral shirts without buttons are there compared to white shirts without collars?","A clothing store has 40 white shirts and 50 floral shirts. Half of the white shirts have collars, and 20 of the floral shirts have buttons. How many more floral shirts with no buttons are there than white shirts with no collars?",10,10,10,10,"Let’s define the quantities first.

