"Marissa’s class has 30 kids and each one got 10 pencils at the start of the year. Two months in, they’d used up 1/5 of all their pencils. By the year's end, only 1/3 of the pencils they had left were still around. How many pencils were left?","There are 30 students in Marissa’s class. Each student started the year with 10 pencils. After two months, 1/5 of the total pencils in class were used. At the end of the year, only 1/3 of the remaining pencils were left. How many pencils were left?",80,80,80,80,"Step 1: Find the total number of pencils at the start.
- 30 kids × 10 pencils each = 300 pencils

Step 2: After two months, they used 1/5 of all pencils.
- Used: (1/5) × 300 = 60
- Remaining: 300 − 60 = 240

Step 3: By year’s end, only 1/3 of the pencils they had left were still around.
- Still around: (1/3) × 240 = 80

